WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.509
Although HBO has been pretty tight-lipped
about Westworld's upcoming third season, they've

00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:08.700
still released a couple of tidbits to keep
fans tided over until the show returns to

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.200
screens.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.260
Here's a round-up of everything we know about
Westworld Season 3.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.660
While the first two seasons of Westworld have
been told mostly from the points of view of

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:21.480
Dolores and the Man in Black, if the first
teaser is any indication, season three seems

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.420
to be taking a sharp turn into something new.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.519
This intriguing glimpse at Westworld's new
season follows a brand new character, played

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:31.539
by Breaking Bad's Aaron Paul, through a series
of events that take place in what appears

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.120
to be the "real" world outside of Delos' park.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.340
From Paul's narration, it sounds as though
the world he inhabits isn't much of an improvement

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.640
on the park, as he talks about his sense that,
although things may look nice on the surface,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.430
that beauty is masking something darker.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.100
Sound like something you've heard before?

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.900
"Some people choose to see the ugliness in
this world.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.360
I choose to see the beauty."

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.240
Paul's character laments that somebody has
made an attempt to smooth over the world's

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:02.129
rough edges, making it all little more than
a "lie," and expresses his hope of finding

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:06.000
something "real," at which point the trailer
finally shows us a familiar face.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.140
Of course, as you probably know from previous
seasons, the men who fall in with Dolores

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.300
are rarely all that they seem…nor do they
ever get what they expect.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.960
Although HBO has yet to announce a premiere
date for season three, don't hold your breath

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.900
on seeing Westworld return to TV screens in
2019.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.160
HBO programming chief Casey Bloys told The
Wrap in early 2019 that production on the

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.700
series' third season was set to begin in March
of the same year.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:33.180
While it's possible that showrunners Jonathan
Nolan and Lisa Joy will race to turn the season

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.060
around before the end of the year, a 2020
premiere date seems more likely.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.920
This would be a slightly longer gap than the
one between the first two seasons, which lasted

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.020
nearly 17 months.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.860
Season one wrapped up in early December of
2016, while season two premiered in late April

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.880
of 2018 and ended in late June.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:53.400
Since season two began filming in the summer
of 2017, that left around 10 months between

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.480
the start of production and the show's premiere.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.780
If the series remains on a similar production
schedule, we could expect to see season three

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.800
as early as January of 2020.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.780
But given the increasingly vast scope of the
series from season to season, it wouldn't

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.780
be a huge surprise if the wait turns out to
be even longer.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.040
"It’s a f------ nightmare.”

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.840
The end of Westworld's second season saw the
park undergo a heap of significant changes,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.720
with a number of important characters dying,
escaping, or transitioning into another reality.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:27.660
Such seismic developments are bound to ripple
out through the show's third season, and if

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.660
the trailer is any indication, the new episodes
will look and feel very different from what's

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:32.360
come before.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.980
"We have to be smarter than them, or they
will find us.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.660
And they will kill us."

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.950
However, not everything will seem strange
and new when Westworld returns for its third

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.440
season, as several main cast members have
already had their returns confirmed.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:53.440
These include the damsel-turned-revolutionary
Dolores Abbernathy, host creator and unwitting

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:58.460
Arnold replica Bernard Lowe, the mysterious
Man in Black, head of security Ashley Stubbs,

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:02.560
the host that looks like Charlotte Hale, and,
somewhat surprisingly, former madam Maeve

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.380
Milla, who sacrificed herself at the end of
season two in order to allow her daughter

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:10.100
a chance to escape the park and enter the
digital utopia of the Sublime.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.880
Of course, everyone knows that death is merely
temporary for the hosts of Westworld, and

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.440
Newton confirmed that she'll be back for season
three in a 2018 interview with Vanity Fair.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.100
"You think I'm scared of death?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.220
I've done it a million times."

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.500
While a number of familiar faces are returning
for season three, the end of season two marked

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.440
a definitive farewell for several others.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.580
Anthony Hopkins' park creator Robert Ford
has been dead since the end of season one

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.891
too, and although he has continued to appear
regularly in flashbacks and visions, according

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.900
to series creator Lisa Joy, he's now gone
for good.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:51.180
"Like I said, I built all of this."

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:56.480
Meanwhile, Jimmi Simpson's character, William,
will still be very much alive in season three,

00:03:56.490 --> 00:04:00.810
but will be portrayed exclusively by Ed Harris,
as Simpson revealed to the Television Critics

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.160
Association that he hasn't been asked to return.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.480
In previous seasons, Harris played the older
William, while Simpson portrayed his younger

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.060
counterpart.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.120
Shannon Woodward's determined truth-seeker
Elsie was tragically murdered at the end of

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:16.540
season two, and Jonathan Nolan has confirmed
that, while "there's never any real saying

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:19.740
goodbye" in Westworld, Elsie is truly gone…for
now, at least.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.340
Less clear is the fate of James Marsden's
stalwart cowboy, Teddy.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:27.980
Introduced in the pilot episode, Teddy spent
the majority of his time on the show as Dolores'

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:32.390
most devoted protector and ally, until he
realized that she had altered his programming.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:36.190
Teddy killed himself near the end of season
two, determined to die rather than become

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:40.410
a monster, but Dolores left his brain pearl
in the Forge, leaving his consciousness free

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.980
to cross over into the Sublime.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:46.520
Nothing has yet been said one way or another
about Marsden's return, but since this is

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.980
Westworld, you should know better than to
rule anything out.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:54.160
Beyond the addition of Breaking Bad's Aaron
Paul to the cast as a series regular, Westworld

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.580
season 3 will see a number of new faces join
the show.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:01.420
These include include Lena Waithe, Vincent
Cassel, rapper Kid Cudi, and former NFL running

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.040
back Marshawn Lynch.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:04.300
"Hey you.”

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:05.040
“Haha.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:05.540
What's up with it?

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.400
Boy what is it you got on that thing?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:12.300
I don't know about that, where I'm from, we
don't wear those."

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:16.100
Judging by the trailer, it seems as though
Waithe and Lynch will be playing Paul's accomplices

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:20.580
in some sort of bank heist, while Cudi's character,
who also seems to have some sort of tie to

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.800
Paul's character, will be spending at least
some of his time in prison.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:29.040
At the end of season two, most of the hosts
either traveled into the Sublime or were destroyed

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:33.420
and reclaimed by Delos, but there are still
a mysterious few whose fates remain undecided.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:37.460
In "The Passenger," Dolores, in the guise
of Charlotte Hale, took five pearl-shaped

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:41.400
control units with her out of the park, each
housing the consciousness of one host.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:45.280
Just which hosts are represented by each of
those control units remain to be seen, and

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.340
according to Jonathan Nolan, not even the
writers had fully decided who was in Dolores'

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:51.000
purse at the end of season two.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.800
Nolan explained to Entertainment Weekly:

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:56.780
"We've had some interesting conversations,
but as always with this show, who remains

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:59.060
and who doesn't is something we're having
a lot of fun with."

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:03.420
Nolan went on to say that, when the inhabitants
of those pearls are eventually revealed, the

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:07.560
goal of the writers is for their choices to
"surprise and hopefully delight" their audience.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:11.400
While you can probably rule out any of the
hosts who crossed into the Sublime, that still

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.300
leaves a large number of hosts to pick from,
so place your bets wisely.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.560
"There is beauty in what we are.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.560
Shouldn't we too try to survive?"

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:27.360
While the earliest episodes of Westworld took
place almost exclusively within the park,

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:31.420
as the series has progressed, so has the scope
of its setting, with much of season two venturing

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:32.460
into the outside world.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.550
Now, with each of the show's principal host
characters all living on the outside, the

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:40.620
showrunners are eager to see what sorts of
storytelling opportunities this vast new setting

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:41.260
opens up.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.380
Joy told The Wrap:

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:44.800
"It was always the plan to explore the real
world.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:48.700
There are three Hosts out in the world and
next season will really be an exploration

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.220
of what they find and who they become."

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:54.160
Given that Dolores and Bernard were two of
the most central characters in season two,

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:57.980
it's probably safe to assume that since they're
both on the outside, season three will wind

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.720
up spending a lot more time outside the walls
of the park.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.780
Add to that the first teaser, which seems
to take place exclusively in the real world,

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:08.510
and it would be reasonable to wonder whether
the Westworld-centric days of Westworld might

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:09.080
be over.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:13.400
Although a few main characters have managed
to escape Ford's world, there are still others

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.900
left on the inside, with several theme parks
remaining unexplored.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:21.650
In addition to Westworld, season two introduced
viewers to Shogunworld and The Raj, but the

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:25.540
show's official Delos Destinations website
teases three additional parks.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:29.300
The site lists no details about them, but
Nolan and Joy have previously hinted that

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:33.790
the show may eventually visit the Roman and
Medieval Worlds from Michael Crichton's original

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.020
1973 movie.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:40.320
As for the sixth world, it could be Futureworld,
which appeared in the 1976 sequel, although

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:43.320
Nolan and Joy could just as easily create
something brand new.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:47.220
In fact, the identity of at least one park
seems to have been confirmed by the Comic-Con

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:47.720
trailer.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:51.960
Although Maeve was last seen shot to death
outside the entrance to the Sublime, the trailer

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:55.480
finds her looking as good as new, in a place
that looks a lot like Nazi-occupied Europe

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:56.500
during World War II.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:59.340
This may very well be a glimpse at one of
the remaining three parks.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:03.450
Although World War II doesn't exactly seem
like a prime vacation spot, if there's one

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:07.520
thing that's clear about the elite clientele
of Delos' theme parks, it's that they're drawn

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:11.620
to violent settings, and how much more violent
can you get than history's deadliest war?

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.300
In an interview with Entertainment Weekly,
Jonathan Nolan and Lisa Joy revealed a few

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:20.870
details about Aaron Paul's previously mysterious
character, hinting that he may be a little

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:25.169
different to the executives, scientists, and
socialites who make up Westworld's cast of

00:08:25.169 --> 00:08:26.160
human characters.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.300
Paul will be playing a Los Angeles construction
worker named Caleb.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:30.660
According to Nolan,

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:33.180
"[He'll be] the type of person who doesn't
get to go to Westworld."

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:37.380
Westworld's first season made it clear that
only the extremely wealthy are able to afford

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:42.490
the hefty $40,000 per day price tag that allows
them to partake in the violent delights of

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:43.720
Delos' themed parks.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.380
Because of this, the only humans that the
hosts of the parks have encountered, up until

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:51.490
this point, have either been employed by Delos,
or have all belonged to the same super-elite

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.380
social class.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:57.060
But now that Dolores is outside of the park,
it sounds like her horizons will become significantly

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:01.540
broadened, and according to Nolan, Caleb will,
quote, "challenge Dolores' notions about the

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:02.700
nature of humanity."

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:07.540
Although artificial lifeforms are nothing
new for Westworld fans, season 3 will nonetheless

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:11.040
introduce a different type of robot to the
hosts who have appeared so far.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:16.020
Shown hanging out with Aaron Paul's construction
worker Caleb in HBO's initial teaser for season

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:20.760
three, George is a standard construction robot,
Delos model G-267.

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:25.460
Built to serve as a helpful co-worker for
Caleb, George doesn't speak, and likely won't

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.880
have much in common with his mechanical counterparts
from inside the park.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.220
In his Entertainment Weekly interview, Nolan
said:

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:34.650
"Part of what our hosts find [is that] they're
caught in between, they're fashioned to look

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:38.580
like human beings and act like them, but they
have more in common with the mechanical pieces

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:39.260
in our world."

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:43.280
Robots like George and the other real-world
worker-bots glimpsed in the full season 3

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:47.350
trailer will play an important role in the
upcoming season, contrasting the human-like

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.440
traits of the hosts with their mechanical
origins.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:54.000
While the hosts have been designed to act
as emotional mirrors to human guests in Delos'

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.560
parks, these more utilitarian robots have
been designed with specific uses in mind.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:09:59.800
"Yeah, science!"

